@node Intro " Introduction"

This is very small (3372 Bytes) AmiExpress XiM Door with the
following features:

- Displays the Nodenumber to which the User is Connected to.
- Displays the Locked Baudrate of the Node.
- Launches a Batch when a User Logs on, so your Logoff Batch
  can be reduced to a very small size and will safe a lot of time.
 
  Note:
  Logon.Batch is executed with the RunBack command in your C: Dir
  so you can have as much Utils as you want in your Batch File!

- Displays if the Sysop is around or not.
- Displays the Serial Device of the Node
- Displays the Number of Nodes available.

This is how it looks like:
--------------------------

.---------------------------------------------------------------------------.
| lOGONINFO v1.o (1oo% ASM) - © 1994 by WHiZ/eNDLESS pIRACY/rEFLEX/tHERAPY! |
+-----------------------+-----------------------+---------------------------+
| Connected to Node #1  | Locked at 115200 Baud | Launching Logon Batch ... |
+-----------------------+-----------------------+---------------------------+
|  Sysop is NOT Around! | DEV: duart.device     | NDZ: XXX                  |
`-----------------------+-----------------------+---------------------------'

How this Util works:
-------------------

When a User Logs on this Util looks for the File "Logon.Batch" in your
BBS: Dir:

- If found, it'll display "Launching Logon Batch" and executes the Batch.
- If Not found, it'll display "Logon Batch Not Found" and continues quietly.

Then it checks if the chatflag is on or off.

- If the Sysop is in, it'll inform the User with the Message
  "Sysop Can Be Paged", that the Sysop is available for Chatting.
- If the Sysop is not around, it'll display "Sysop is NOT Around!"


                         @{"     Main Menu      " Link MAIN}

@endnode
@node Require " Requirements"

All you need to run this little Util is:

- An Amiga, no matter which model.
- Should work on Ami- or Sigma-Express version! (But only tested
  on /X v3.37 & v3.38)
- AEDoor.library v2.0+ by SiNTAX/WøT
- RunBack Command in your C: Dir.
- Logon.Batch in your BBS: Dir, protected with +s

Thats all...

                         @{"     Main Menu      " Link MAIN}

@endnode
@node Install " Installation"

- If you don't have the AEDoor.library (v2.0+) by SiNTAX/WøT in your LIBS
  dir already just copy the version included in this archive to your
  LIBS Dir.

- This little Door also requires the RunBack Command in your C: Dir.
  If you don't have this command just copy the version included in
  this archive to your C: Dir.

- This Door is executed via the FrontEnd.info icon. Either copy
  the FrontEnd.info icon included in this archive to your
  BBS:Commands/SYSCmd/ Dir or create a new FrontEnd.info icon with the
  following Tooltypes:

  LOCATION=DOORS:LogonInfo
  TYPE=XIM
  MULTINODE=YES
  STACK=4096
  ACCESS=001

- Now create a Batch called BBS:Logon.Batch, and protect it with +s
  for instance: Protect BBS:Logon.Batch +s
 
                        That's it folks ...

  This Util has been tested for a couple of weeks without any crashs
  or problems at all! Give my Board a Ring and see for yourself!

  Thanks to Joker/ZZC & DEXter!/AFL for Beta-Testing!  

  If you should find any Bugs or have any Suggestions, feel free to
  contact me on PSYCHO TERMiNAL +1(914)682-1975 or via /XNet WHiZ@203001


